ce":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Iddo","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":6,"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.15","rawReference":"2Chr.12.15"}],"ruleId":"Iddo::Iddo::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Iddo"},"text":"Now the acts of Rehoboam, from first to last, are they not written in the records of Shemaiah the Prophet and of Iddo the Seer concerning the genealogies? There was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam throughout their days.","verse":15}],"id":"Iddo","label":"Iddo","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Iddo::Iddo::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Iddo","term":"Iddo"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Iddo","sourceTitle":"Iddo"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"In the fifth year of Rehoboam’s reign, because they had been unfaithful to the LORD, Shishak king of Egypt attacked Jerusalem","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"He captured the fortified cities of Judah and came as far as Jerusalem.","verse":4},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"Then Shemaiah the prophet came to Rehoboam and the leaders of Judah who had gathered at Jerusalem because of Shishak, and he said to them, “This is what the LORD says: ‘You have forsaken Me; therefore, I have forsaken you into the hand of Shishak.’”","verse":5},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"When the LORD saw that they had humbled themselves, the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah, saying, “They have humbled themselves; I will not destroy them, but will soon grant them deliverance. My wrath will not be poured out on Jerusalem through Shishak.","verse":7},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"So King Shishak of Egypt attacked Jerusalem and seized the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the royal palace. He took everything, including the gold shields that Solomon had made.","verse":9},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Jerusalem","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem"},"text":"Thus King Rehoboam established himself in Jerusalem and reigned. He was forty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city the LORD had chosen from all the tribes of Israel in which to put His Name. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonite.","verse":13}],"id":"Jerusalem","label":"Jerusalem","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Jerusalem::Jerusalem::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Jerusalem","term":"Jerusalem"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Jerusalem","sourceTitle":"Jerusalem"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"After Rehoboam had established his sovereignty and royal power, he and all Israel with him forsook the Law of the LORD.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"In the fifth year of Rehoboam’s reign, because they had been unfaithful to the LORD, Shishak king of Egypt attacked Jerusalem","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Then Shemaiah the prophet came to Rehoboam and the leaders of Judah who had gathered at Jerusalem because of Shishak, and he said to them, “This is what the LORD says: ‘You have forsaken Me; therefore, I have forsaken you into the hand of Shishak.’”","verse":5},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"So the leaders of Israel and the king humbled themselves and said, “The LORD is righteous.”","verse":6},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"When the LORD saw that they had humbled themselves, the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah, saying, “They have humbled themselves; I will not destroy them, but will soon grant them deliverance. My wrath will not be poured out on Jerusalem through Shishak.","verse":7},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"So King Shishak of Egypt attacked Jerusalem and seized the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the royal palace. He took everything, including the gold shields that Solomon had made.","verse":9},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"And whenever the king entered the house of the LORD, the guards would go with him, bearing the shields, and later they would return them to the guardroom.","verse":11},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Because Rehoboam humbled himself, the anger of the LORD turned away from him, and He did not destroy him completely. Indeed, conditions were good in Judah.","verse":12},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Thus King Rehoboam established himself in Jerusalem and reigned. He was forty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city the LORD had chosen from all the tribes of Israel in which to put His Name. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonite.","verse":13},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"And Rehoboam did evil because he did not set his heart to seek the LORD.","verse":14}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Rehoboam","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":5,"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.1","rawReference":"2Chr.12.1"}],"ruleId":"Rehoboam::Rehoboam::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Rehoboam"},"text":"After Rehoboam had established his sovereignty and royal power, he and all Israel with him forsook the Law of the LORD.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Rehoboam","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":9,"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.2-3","rawReference":"2Chr.12.2-3"}],"ruleId":"Rehoboam::Rehoboam::source_v